LESSON 3: PULLING BOOK DATA FROM A DIFFERENT DATA FILE
================================================================================

PART 1: OVERVIEW OF THE LESSON
================================================================================

WHAT YOU'LL LEARN IN THIS LESSON
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This lesson focuses on separating data from components and managing data
in external files.

You will understand:

• Why separating data from components is important

• How to create a separate data file for book information

• Importing data from external files into components

• Managing data structure and organization

• Best practices for data file organization

• Handling large datasets efficiently

• Scaling applications with external data sources

• Preparing for API integration

• Maintaining clean component code

• Improving code reusability and maintainability


WHY SEPARATING DATA FROM COMPONENTS MATTERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Separating data from components is important because:

• Improves Maintainability
  - Data changes can be made separately from component presentation logic

• Enables Scalability
  - More static data can be added without cluttering component files

• Facilitates Testing
  - Components can receive different data during testing

• Supports Collaboration
  - Developers can work on different areas of the project

• Prepares for APIs
  - Makes the transition from static data to API-provided data clearer

• Reduces Component Complexity
  - Components can focus on rendering and behavior

• Enables Independent Data Optimization
  - Data organization can be improved separately from component code

• Enables Data Reuse
  - The same data can be imported into multiple modules

• Simplifies Debugging
  - Clear separation makes responsibilities easier to identify

• Follows Separation of Concerns
  - Data and presentation responsibilities remain distinct


