================================================================================
PART 4: CREATING A DATA INDEX FILE
================================================================================

WHY CREATE A DATA INDEX FILE?
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

A data index file can:

• Centralize Exports
  - Exposes selected data modules from one file

• Simplify Imports
  - Consumers can import through the data directory

• Support Refactoring
  - Internal paths are managed by the index file

• Improve Readability
  - Creates cleaner import statements

• Define a Public API
  - Makes available data modules easy to identify


CREATE THE DATA INDEX FILE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Create:

src/data/index.js


CODE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// Export books data

export { default as booksData } from './books'


// You can add more data exports here as needed

// export { default as usersData } from './users'
// export { default as categoriesData } from './categories'


WHAT THIS FILE DOES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Exports booksData

• Centralizes data exports

• Supports adding additional data files

• Enables cleaner imports elsewhere


WITHOUT INDEX FILE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

import booksData from './data/books'


WITH INDEX FILE:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

import { booksData } from './data'


