PART 10: COMMON MISTAKES TO AVOID
================================================================================

MISTAKE 1: MIXING LARGE STATIC DATASETS WITH COMPONENTS
================================================================================

LESS ORGANIZED APPROACH:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// App.jsx with hardcoded data

export default function App() {

  const [books, setBooks] = useState([
    {
      id: 1,
      title: 'Book 1'
      // ...
    },
    {
      id: 2,
      title: 'Book 2'
      // ...
    }

    // Many more books...
  ])

  // Component logic mixed with data
}


BETTER-SEPARATED APPROACH:
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// books.js

const booksData = [
  {
    id: 1,
    title: 'Book 1'
    // ...
  },
  {
    id: 2,
    title: 'Book 2'
    // ...
  }
]

export default booksData


// App.jsx

import { booksData } from './data'

export default function App() {

  const [books, setBooks] = useState(booksData)

  // Component logic
}


WHY IT MATTERS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

• Cleaner Component Code

• Easier Maintenance

• Better Organization

• Clearer Separation of Concerns


